🛠️ LearnMate AI – Technology Stack

1. Overview

LearnMate AI is planned as an AI-powered personalized learning platform using modern web technologies and artificial intelligence.

The technology stack will support an interactive frontend, backend processing, AI-powered assistance, and student progress management.

2. Proposed Technologies

Technology| Purpose
HTML5| Frontend structure
CSS3| Styling and responsive design
JavaScript| Interactive functionality
Python| Backend development
Flask| Backend framework
Gemini API| AI-powered explanations and assistance
SQLite| Database management
Git & GitHub| Version control and collaboration

3. Technology Details

Frontend

- HTML5 for page structure.
- CSS3 for responsive user interface.
- JavaScript for interactive features.

Backend

- Python for application logic.
- Flask for handling backend requests and application routes.

Artificial Intelligence

- Gemini API for generating educational explanations.
- AI-based assistance for personalized learning recommendations.
- AI-generated practice questions.

Database

- SQLite for storing student information, quiz results, learning activities, and progress.

Version Control

- Git for tracking development changes.
- GitHub for source code management and project documentation.

4. Proposed System Architecture

The planned application workflow:

1. Student interacts with the frontend.
2. Frontend sends requests to the backend.
3. Backend processes student assessment data.
4. AI services assist with explanations and recommendations.
5. Database stores relevant learning progress.
6. Personalized results are displayed to the student.

5. Future Technology Improvements

Depending on project requirements, we may explore:

- Advanced learning analytics.
- Voice-based interaction.
- Multilingual AI support.
- Progressive Web App capabilities.
- Offline learning support.

6. Development Status

Current Stage: Project documentation and initial planning.

The technologies listed above are proposed choices. Their actual integration and implementation will be completed progressively.

